   "stem": {
      "text": "A particle moves along the x-axis with velocity \\( v(t) = - 6 t^{2} - 6 t + 6 \\) meters per second, where t is measured in seconds, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). At time t = 1 the position of the particle is \\( x(1) = -4 \\) meters. Find the position of the particle at time t = 3.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -68,
      "units": "meters"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Position changes by the integral of velocity, so \\( x(3) = x(1) + \\int_{1}^{3} v(t)\\,dt \\).",
         "rule_named": "position from velocity by accumulation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "An antiderivative of v is \\( - 2 t^{3} - 3 t^{2} + 6 t \\), so \\( \\int_{1}^{3} v(t)\\,dt = \\left[- 2 t^{3} - 3 t^{2} + 6 t\\right]_{1}^{3} = -64 \\).",
         "mathjson": -64,
         "rule_named": "fundamental theorem of calculus"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Add the known position: \\( x(3) = x(1) + \\int_{1}^{3} v(t)\\,dt = -4 - 64 = -68 \\) meters.",
         "mathjson": -68,
         "rule_named": "add the initial position"
      }
   ],
